WEBVTT

00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:47.720
Ow!

00:00:51.080 --> 00:00:56.640
There's supposed to be a chair there.

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:59.800
It's the chair's fault you can't sit down(!)

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:01.720
Look what my aunt sent me.

00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:03.400
Wicked!

00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:06.360
Not exactly a healthy breakfast.

00:01:05.480 --> 00:01:10.800
Where have all the cereals gone?

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:11.840
Oh, what?!

00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:12.440
Look!

00:01:11.720 --> 00:01:14.040
It's happened again.

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:15.920
Just like yesterday.

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:17.520
What...?

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:19.400
This is getting weird.

00:01:18.520 --> 00:01:21.880
Maybe it's burglars.

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:24.560
They steal, not rearrange.

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:28.600
Maybe it's the type of... makeover burglars!

00:01:27.640 --> 00:01:28.920
What about wolves?

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:30.360
Did you just say wolves?

00:01:29.480 --> 00:01:34.400
OK, not wolves but...bears!

00:01:33.440 --> 00:01:38.040
What about...ghosts?

00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:39.160
Please!

00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:42.040
Who do you think's moving the stuff about, Tracy?

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:44.240
Bears or ghosts?

00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:48.000
Interesting question, Bouncer, but I don't have time to answer it.

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:54.840
Cam's got tickets to an exclusive screening of a Hollywood movie.

00:01:54.440 --> 00:02:00.160
Big smile.

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:08.320
And tonight's premiere will star Tracy's mum!

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:22.680
Adele told me to tell you that Cam rang and she can't make it.

00:02:21.800 --> 00:02:23.960
What?

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:24.920
Oh, yeah!

00:02:23.960 --> 00:02:26.640
Oh, yeah!

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:29.200
I'm not really that bothered.

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:34.120
I hate limos and tiaras and movie stars.

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:34.480
It's all so...phoney.

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:37.480
Yeah, course it is.

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:41.520
Why did you stand me up?

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:42.240
I'm sorry.

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:42.960
Me too.

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:44.920
What's going on?

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:46.480
Tracy, I'm ill.

00:02:45.560 --> 00:02:53.440
My headache feels like a car alarm going off, my stomach won't stop... and I've got a temperature.

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:54.200
I feel awful.

00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:55.400
Oh, right.

00:02:54.760 --> 00:02:57.000
Oh, dear, Cam.

00:02:56.160 --> 00:02:59.200
Well, it's lucky I've come round.

00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:01.280
You'll get the full service.

00:03:00.520 --> 00:03:04.480
Tracy, thanks, but I really need some rest.

00:03:03.640 --> 00:03:06.800
I will see you when I'm better, OK.

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:15.120
Ben, I need blankets, medicines and home comforts.

00:03:14.280 --> 00:03:18.160
We'll raid the Dumping Ground.

00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:20.200
Of course Cam needs my help!

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:22.040
She just hasn't realised it.

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:24.560
She doesn't have faith in the skills of Dr Beaker.

00:03:59.120 --> 00:04:00.760
What could be so important...?

00:03:59.880 --> 00:04:02.600
Delivery for Miss Wilson!

00:04:02.040 --> 00:04:04.760
Tracy, what...?

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:05.920
You need looking after.

00:04:05.360 --> 00:04:12.040
I checked the internet and the medical dictionary.

00:04:11.080 --> 00:04:16.480
You've either got an Amazonian stomach snake, or flu.

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:28.560
Just to be safe, I'm prescribing bed rest, a nice warm temperature, plenty of liquids, vitamin-filled meals and plenty of sleep and a chocolate bar you can use as a desk!

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:30.440
Tracy, I'm all right.

00:04:29.560 --> 00:04:31.120
I don't need your help.

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:33.360
I just need quiet.

00:04:32.520 --> 00:04:34.520
OK.

00:04:33.560 --> 00:04:36.360
If you don't need my help, I'll go.

00:04:35.600 --> 00:04:39.520
(She's delirious. )

00:04:43.040 --> 00:04:46.080
Who's got it?

00:04:45.440 --> 00:04:48.920
I don't care what the story is, I want it back NOW!

00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:49.560
What?

00:04:48.640 --> 00:04:52.400
The present from my aunt - my chocolate bar?

00:04:51.800 --> 00:04:56.280
It's hard to lose, so who's got it?

00:04:55.320 --> 00:04:58.280
Oh, I get it!

00:04:57.720 --> 00:05:00.720
I get the blame for everything.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:01.880
Has anyone noticed Tracy borrowing things?

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:06.920
She took my pillow and a plant.

00:05:13.720 --> 00:05:17.080
Nothing.

00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:22.960
She's probably taken it away to eat it all and get rid of the evidence.

00:05:22.360 --> 00:05:24.280
Who's going to tell Jenny?

00:05:23.440 --> 00:05:25.280
No-one.

00:05:24.640 --> 00:05:29.120
Walking furniture... moving cereal...

00:05:28.520 --> 00:05:32.240
There's more to this than chocolate theft.

00:05:31.320 --> 00:05:36.440
I just need a chance to solve the mystery of...the Nightstalker.

00:05:35.560 --> 00:05:37.600
"Nightstalker."

00:05:36.760 --> 00:05:39.040
Yeah, I like it.

00:05:38.080 --> 00:05:40.480
Count me in.

00:05:39.680 --> 00:05:45.120
Nightstalker's gonna get stalked.

00:05:44.360 --> 00:05:47.520
We'll all sleep safer in our beds tonight(!)

00:05:49.080 --> 00:05:50.560
Hi, there.

00:05:49.640 --> 00:05:54.680
I'm here to see the...person in charge.

00:05:53.800 --> 00:05:58.880
You mean Mr Byron?

00:05:58.040 --> 00:06:00.920
Delivery for My Byron.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:01.160
Hello.

00:06:00.520 --> 00:06:04.240
I've got the next children's bestseller here.

00:06:03.280 --> 00:06:08.400
You can read it, but I advise you to just start the adverts now.

00:06:07.520 --> 00:06:12.280
I'm a typical kid and I loved it.

00:06:25.120 --> 00:06:28.680
It's just gone 0300 hours.

00:06:28.040 --> 00:06:29.280
Perhaps we should go downstairs.

00:06:28.560 --> 00:06:30.280
No.

00:06:29.400 --> 00:06:30.480
Go to bed.

00:06:29.520 --> 00:06:32.800
Shut up, Bounce!

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:36.000
The Nightstalker's not here.

00:06:35.240 --> 00:06:39.480
CREAKING The Nightstalker!

00:06:38.600 --> 00:06:41.840
The cricket bat!

00:06:41.160 --> 00:06:42.720
YOU use it.

00:06:41.760 --> 00:06:43.960
You asked for it!

00:06:43.160 --> 00:06:44.920
To make sure you had it.

00:06:44.120 --> 00:06:45.840
Yeah, but...

00:06:44.960 --> 00:06:48.640
Aaaaargh!

00:06:49.640 --> 00:06:53.600
Keep the noise down, boys.

00:06:52.840 --> 00:07:06.520
The Nightstalker might hear you.

00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:14.640
(Louise. )

00:07:13.840 --> 00:07:15.560
(Hey, Lou!

00:07:14.840 --> 00:07:17.360
Louise!)

00:07:16.400 --> 00:07:21.000
What...what time is it?

00:07:20.080 --> 00:07:21.560
5.15.

00:07:20.680 --> 00:07:23.160
I heard creaking downstairs.

00:07:22.280 --> 00:07:25.040
I think it's Tracy, up to her tricks again.

00:07:24.120 --> 00:07:26.040
Come on!

00:07:25.080 --> 00:07:27.200
Come on!

00:07:29.800 --> 00:07:35.840
Tracy's going to be so embarrassed once we catch her out!

00:07:35.520 --> 00:07:40.400
Lol!

00:07:47.920 --> 00:07:51.360
It was SO funny!

00:07:51.320 --> 00:07:53.000
He was like the mummy!

00:07:52.080 --> 00:07:53.480
Yeah, well...

00:07:52.520 --> 00:07:57.480
I was just putting it on to fool you.

00:07:57.120 --> 00:07:58.560
It worked a treat.

00:07:57.720 --> 00:08:02.080
So, why did you let us put that necklace on you?

00:08:01.120 --> 00:08:04.760
Yeah, you really... (!)

00:08:03.800 --> 00:08:05.080
That was stupid.

00:08:04.120 --> 00:08:09.640
You're not meant to do anything to wake a sleepwalker.

00:08:08.720 --> 00:08:11.760
Right.

00:08:10.920 --> 00:08:12.000
Ha!

00:08:22.280 --> 00:08:27.680
"You need vitamin C."

00:08:28.880 --> 00:08:34.679
"Thank you for submitting your manuscript, but it's not for us..."

00:08:34.360 --> 00:08:36.000
It's a bargain price.

00:08:35.159 --> 00:08:42.240
My foster mother's ill, but she's a writer, so we need something with more pizzazz.

00:08:41.480 --> 00:08:42.880
Tracy!

00:08:41.919 --> 00:08:45.039
Oh, hi, Cam.

00:08:44.159 --> 00:08:45.640
Feeling better?

00:08:44.840 --> 00:08:48.280
This is a rejection for my children's book.

00:08:48.640 --> 00:08:50.960
Oh, I'm sorry...

00:08:50.120 --> 00:08:52.160
For sale?!

00:08:51.360 --> 00:08:54.640
Better luck next time.

00:08:53.720 --> 00:08:56.240
The book I hadn't finished yet.

00:08:55.320 --> 00:08:59.040
I have to do everything for you!

00:08:58.240 --> 00:09:00.320
Tracy, don't push it.

00:09:00.200 --> 00:09:05.200
My mum used to be this interfering and that's why I left home at 15.

00:09:04.360 --> 00:09:07.800
At least I try to look after you!

00:09:07.040 --> 00:09:10.080
Hey, I did try.

00:09:09.200 --> 00:09:12.280
It just didn't work out, that's all.

00:09:11.480 --> 00:09:13.240
OK.

00:09:12.280 --> 00:09:16.680
Well, you're not my mum and I'm not yours, so leave it at that!

00:09:17.880 --> 00:09:20.480
Anyone want clothes?

00:09:19.720 --> 00:09:22.680
Tracy had a clear-out.

00:09:21.840 --> 00:09:25.960
I've got some for my fashion project on the '80s.

00:09:26.280 --> 00:09:34.440
You should see what Tracy took Cam - fruit and the biggest chocolate bar.

00:09:33.680 --> 00:09:36.440
Did you just say "chocolate"?

00:09:35.600 --> 00:09:40.280
I can't believe Tracy nicked it.

00:09:39.360 --> 00:09:44.240
Can't trust anyone with that hair.

00:09:43.760 --> 00:09:45.960
Guess what...?

00:09:45.160 --> 00:09:48.960
Um, I was gonna tell you.

00:09:48.120 --> 00:09:49.800
I found it in...

00:09:48.920 --> 00:09:50.640
Tracy's room.

00:09:49.800 --> 00:09:51.480
Yeah, right(!)

00:09:56.000 --> 00:09:59.400
You...chocolate thief!

00:10:02.640 --> 00:10:04.080
Hi, Cam.

00:10:03.120 --> 00:10:05.760
Hello, Tracy.

00:10:04.880 --> 00:10:13.160
I want to say, about the books, the clothes, the chocolates... actually, that was Ben, but everything else...

00:10:12.520 --> 00:10:13.640
Yep?

00:10:12.680 --> 00:10:16.600
I want to say I'm not sorry.

00:10:15.760 --> 00:10:17.200
NOT sorry?

00:10:16.280 --> 00:10:18.400
No.

00:10:17.560 --> 00:10:21.200
I was trying to do my best for you.

00:10:20.320 --> 00:10:24.520
I'll always do anything I can for you, so I'm not sorry.

00:10:23.560 --> 00:10:25.000
Right.

00:10:24.080 --> 00:10:26.520
Great(!)

00:10:25.720 --> 00:10:34.280
Well, you were wrong and you tried to take over my life and got it all wrong, so...non-apology not accepted.

00:10:33.320 --> 00:10:34.520
OK.

00:10:33.720 --> 00:10:36.200
Good.

00:10:35.280 --> 00:10:41.360
Now we haven't got that sorted, I've got some tickets to another press screening.

00:10:42.000 --> 00:10:44.480
I could squeeze it into my schedule.

00:10:43.600 --> 00:10:46.240
Excellent.

00:10:45.600 --> 00:10:56.240
I've replenished my wardrobe from a charity shop, so I'll be wearing this.

00:11:06.760 --> 00:11:14.800
Lol?

00:11:19.240 --> 00:11:20.760
Bouncer!

00:11:21.480 --> 00:11:27.160
Don't wake...the sleepwalker.

00:11:26.360 --> 00:11:31.280
Dangerous to wake... the sleepwalker.

00:11:30.360 --> 00:11:38.960
Nice try, but sleepwalkers don't get the highest score on Death Raid.

00:11:38.920 --> 00:11:42.680
Louise, go on, a bit more!

00:11:42.120 --> 00:11:45.240
That piece is tiny!

00:11:44.320 --> 00:11:49.360
I know, but this way it'll last.

00:11:48.520 --> 00:11:51.840
CRASHING What was that?

00:11:50.880 --> 00:11:53.520
Let's go and see.

00:11:52.640 --> 00:11:54.760
We'd better be quiet.

00:11:53.840 --> 00:11:56.160
I know!

00:11:55.360 --> 00:11:57.640
Quiet, Louise.

00:11:56.680 --> 00:11:59.160
OW!

00:11:58.440 --> 00:12:00.920
Justine, shut up!

00:12:02.960 --> 00:12:04.040
Louise...

00:12:04.880 --> 00:12:06.360
Justine...

00:12:09.360 --> 00:12:11.640
Lol!

00:12:11.040 --> 00:12:15.640
Let's get him!

00:12:15.320 --> 00:12:18.480
I can't believe this has happened.

00:12:17.520 --> 00:12:19.800
Where am I?

00:12:19.160 --> 00:12:23.360
Why are you two so wet?

00:12:22.560 --> 00:12:23.680
- Lol!

00:12:22.800 --> 00:12:24.600
This is so weird.

00:12:23.760 --> 00:12:26.640
I'm so sorry.

00:12:26.360 --> 00:12:27.640
LOL!

00:12:30.680 --> 00:12:34.200
How do you annoy an adult?

00:12:33.360 --> 00:12:35.960
Watch and learn!

00:12:36.880 --> 00:12:40.280
I was here first!

00:12:39.360 --> 00:12:41.040
I bagsied it at breakfast!

00:12:40.160 --> 00:12:43.600
I never heard you!

00:12:42.680 --> 00:12:45.600
You were stuck under your duvet!

00:12:44.640 --> 00:12:48.520
Anyone who starts fighting stays here!

00:12:47.680 --> 00:12:56.320
I worked hard to get you on this day trip for deprived city kids.

00:12:55.480 --> 00:12:59.720
Act more deprived and less cocky!

00:12:58.880 --> 00:13:02.160
I'll see my first sheep!

00:13:01.320 --> 00:13:04.160
It's Lara Croft!

00:13:03.280 --> 00:13:05.360
Shut it, Justine!

00:13:04.520 --> 00:13:06.960
Do we need the rope?

00:13:06.040 --> 00:13:09.320
It pays to be prepared, my mum says.

00:13:08.360 --> 00:13:10.160
Here we go.

00:13:09.400 --> 00:13:13.080
My mum's explored the world.

00:13:12.120 --> 00:13:16.080
She's taken me to places not on any map.

00:13:27.280 --> 00:13:30.840
Leave the line, Tracy!

00:13:29.920 --> 00:13:34.240
What if I need to rescue someone from quicksand?!

00:13:33.360 --> 00:13:34.640
Fair point.

00:13:34.640 --> 00:13:37.440
Sure you don't want to come?

00:13:36.560 --> 00:13:39.160
You organised it.

00:13:38.240 --> 00:13:40.640
Someone's got to hold down the fort.

00:13:39.720 --> 00:13:44.280
I've got some paperwork to do so...

00:13:45.200 --> 00:13:47.280
Are you ready, kids?

00:13:46.360 --> 00:13:50.480
Bye, Jenny!

00:13:53.440 --> 00:13:54.600
Bye!

00:13:56.920 --> 00:13:58.320
Yes!

00:13:57.560 --> 00:14:03.680
A whole day to myself and it was worth it!

00:14:12.360 --> 00:14:14.280
Is this it?

00:14:14.120 --> 00:14:19.480
GOAT BLEATS A field in the middle of nowhere.

00:14:18.560 --> 00:14:22.800
Not exactly Alton Towers, is it?

00:14:22.040 --> 00:14:23.560
Come on, let 'em know we're here!

00:14:23.600 --> 00:14:24.800
Wey-hey!

00:14:23.840 --> 00:14:30.000
Was it something you put in their cornflakes?

00:14:29.200 --> 00:14:30.480
No.

00:14:29.560 --> 00:14:32.960
They're just like spring lambs.

00:14:32.680 --> 00:14:36.600
You must be the lot from Stowey House.

00:14:35.640 --> 00:14:37.440
Ready for action?

00:14:37.080 --> 00:14:38.520
Oh... !

00:14:37.640 --> 00:14:41.080
I was thinking you'd all be boys.

00:14:40.280 --> 00:14:42.680
Of course, girls get put in...

00:14:41.760 --> 00:14:45.240
I mean anyone can end up in...

00:14:44.360 --> 00:14:46.880
Yeah, well, hello to you, too.

00:14:46.040 --> 00:14:47.400
Welcome.

00:14:47.880 --> 00:14:49.160
This is Nathan.

00:14:48.280 --> 00:14:52.480
Gordon Hagley.

00:14:51.600 --> 00:14:55.280
Farmer, man and boy.

00:14:54.400 --> 00:15:01.400
We provide new experiences for people who hardly ever get into the country.

00:15:00.640 --> 00:15:04.240
And this is your field of dreams!

00:15:03.440 --> 00:15:07.760
Let's start with the assault course.

00:15:06.880 --> 00:15:08.240
Assault course?

00:15:07.280 --> 00:15:09.040
Wicked!

00:15:10.240 --> 00:15:13.440
Where are the animals?

00:15:16.440 --> 00:15:21.080
My son Warren built it.

00:15:20.120 --> 00:15:23.360
Don't you worry your pretty heads.

00:15:22.400 --> 00:15:23.520
There's something for everyone.

00:15:22.720 --> 00:15:27.360
There's an animal petting enclosure.

00:15:26.600 --> 00:15:30.640
- WE can go on the assault course!

00:15:30.520 --> 00:15:31.680
Yeah!

00:15:30.760 --> 00:15:31.960
..

00:15:31.160 --> 00:15:33.600
Is it very dirty?

00:15:32.720 --> 00:15:34.520
- Oh, do me a favour!

00:15:33.720 --> 00:15:36.840
You have to be fit!

00:15:36.040 --> 00:15:40.400
You get out of breath watching football!

00:15:39.520 --> 00:15:42.840
Us girls will beat you!

00:15:42.080 --> 00:15:45.000
It's only built for two at a time.

00:15:44.200 --> 00:15:47.120
Me and Louise will be on a team.

00:15:46.160 --> 00:15:48.520
Adele and I will beat you!

00:15:47.560 --> 00:15:50.200
Easy!

00:15:49.360 --> 00:15:50.880
Wait...

00:15:49.960 --> 00:15:52.560
I want to see the animals!

00:15:51.600 --> 00:15:55.400
I'll get Warren to show you.

00:15:54.440 --> 00:15:57.200
I'll just sort these two out.

00:15:58.320 --> 00:16:00.320
Right!

00:16:00.280 --> 00:16:02.400
Come on, on your feet!

00:16:01.520 --> 00:16:04.600
Out here, we lead by example!

00:16:04.720 --> 00:16:05.800
Now...

00:16:04.920 --> 00:16:14.480
I'm timing you!

00:16:15.200 --> 00:16:23.640
"..Leave a message and we'll get back to you.

00:16:22.800 --> 00:16:24.240
Bye."

00:16:23.400 --> 00:16:25.520
BEEP "It's Elaine.

00:16:24.600 --> 00:16:27.480
Jenny, can you pick up, please?

00:16:26.800 --> 00:16:31.080
"My battery's running low and I need to speak...

00:16:30.240 --> 00:16:32.800
Kevin, put those down!

00:16:31.960 --> 00:16:34.480
"Did you swallow one of those?

00:16:33.520 --> 00:16:36.200
Put them down..."

00:16:35.360 --> 00:16:39.880
Why should I suffer when they're off having fun?

00:16:39.200 --> 00:16:43.880
"If you get this message, call me straight back."

00:16:43.800 --> 00:16:47.200
Come on, find the inner you!

00:16:47.400 --> 00:16:55.280
The inner me will be the outer me in a minute!

00:16:54.600 --> 00:16:58.120
Ahhh!

00:16:58.320 --> 00:17:09.680
LOUD RAP MUSIC Who taped over my Schubert?!

00:17:11.359 --> 00:17:24.640
No way!

00:17:23.680 --> 00:17:25.079
Count me out!

00:17:24.119 --> 00:17:26.160
We're a team!

00:17:26.200 --> 00:17:30.120
I'm not here to join the SAS!

00:17:29.280 --> 00:17:31.680
I can't win on my own!

00:17:30.760 --> 00:17:32.720
You'll find a way to level the playing field.

00:17:32.080 --> 00:17:35.120
What?!

00:17:34.240 --> 00:17:36.520
A way to beat them!

00:17:36.080 --> 00:17:39.760
Pitiful!

00:17:39.680 --> 00:17:43.240
You'll have no trouble beating that!

00:17:42.320 --> 00:17:43.760
Even the girls!

00:17:42.800 --> 00:17:45.800
Come on!

00:17:45.360 --> 00:17:48.080
You can hold him.

00:17:47.120 --> 00:17:48.840
Don't be shy.

00:17:48.000 --> 00:17:49.440
Aw, he's so cute!

00:17:48.640 --> 00:17:50.800
Isn't he?

00:17:50.120 --> 00:17:54.920
This a private petting or can anyone join in?

00:17:53.960 --> 00:17:56.160
This is Warren.

00:17:55.200 --> 00:17:56.400
Hi.

00:17:55.480 --> 00:17:57.040
He's showing me his rabbits.

00:17:56.080 --> 00:18:00.760
Hey, rabbit Warren!

00:17:59.840 --> 00:18:04.480
He's showing me loads of animals, but these are babies.

00:18:03.520 --> 00:18:06.520
Where are the grown-up ones?

00:18:06.440 --> 00:18:09.240
Ah, well, um...er...

00:18:08.520 --> 00:18:11.440
You know what happens on a farm?

00:18:10.480 --> 00:18:15.480
They milk cows and grow stuff!

00:18:14.680 --> 00:18:20.160
Where do sausages and chicken nuggets come from?

00:18:19.480 --> 00:18:24.560
Everyone knows that, silly!

00:18:23.760 --> 00:18:25.120
A packet!

00:18:24.320 --> 00:18:26.760
Dolly, they come from a farm like this.

00:18:25.800 --> 00:18:28.560
Where's the rest of your lot?

00:18:27.600 --> 00:18:31.680
Dying on the assault course!

00:18:30.920 --> 00:18:34.400
I built it.

00:18:33.520 --> 00:18:35.360
Did you?

00:18:34.560 --> 00:18:37.240
I'm dying to try it out!

00:18:36.400 --> 00:18:37.880
Yeah?

00:18:37.040 --> 00:18:38.600
I'll take you round.

00:18:37.760 --> 00:18:39.120
Cool.

00:18:38.720 --> 00:18:42.680
Maybe you can show me the farm first.

00:18:41.720 --> 00:18:43.280
Yeah.

00:18:47.600 --> 00:18:50.520
You're free!

00:18:49.920 --> 00:18:53.920
Don't worry, I'll rescue your friends.

00:18:52.960 --> 00:18:54.040
Quick!

00:18:53.240 --> 00:18:56.320
Before they make you into rabbit nuggets!

00:18:57.120 --> 00:19:00.200
I'm timing this.

00:18:59.280 --> 00:19:00.520
I'll send you off staggered.

00:18:59.600 --> 00:19:03.640
First team...go!

00:19:02.840 --> 00:19:05.600
Go on, Bouncer!

00:19:04.680 --> 00:19:07.960
Go on, Bouncer!

00:19:07.200 --> 00:19:09.640
Go on, go on!

00:19:08.760 --> 00:19:09.920
Go on, Bouncer!

00:19:08.960 --> 00:19:12.040
Not bad for city kids.

00:19:11.080 --> 00:19:12.240
They'll never keep it up.

00:19:11.440 --> 00:19:13.480
How do you know?

00:19:12.640 --> 00:19:16.160
Cos I pegged the end of the tunnel down.

00:19:15.200 --> 00:19:16.600
By heck!

00:19:16.120 --> 00:19:18.720
Ahhhh!

00:19:17.760 --> 00:19:20.760
I'm stuck!

00:19:21.360 --> 00:19:24.840
Tracy!

00:19:23.960 --> 00:19:26.640
Wanna start again?

00:19:25.760 --> 00:19:28.640
No, we'll go later.

00:19:28.000 --> 00:19:31.560
Right...next team, go!

00:19:30.720 --> 00:19:33.440
Go on, Tracy!

00:19:32.640 --> 00:19:35.720
Over the head, Tracy!

00:19:34.760 --> 00:19:35.920
That's it!

00:19:35.920 --> 00:19:39.800
Right, last team, go!

00:19:39.000 --> 00:19:41.800
Go on!

00:19:43.520 --> 00:19:46.280
THE GIRLS SCREAM Tracy Beaker!

00:19:48.600 --> 00:19:51.360
- This'll sort out Tracy!

00:19:50.560 --> 00:19:53.680
Good thinking!

00:19:52.960 --> 00:19:56.000
Don't just stand there daydreaming!

00:19:55.120 --> 00:19:57.720
Don't hang around, work as a team!

00:19:57.160 --> 00:19:59.320
- Up and over!

00:19:59.040 --> 00:20:01.520
That guy's a nutter!

00:20:02.000 --> 00:20:03.280
Come on!

00:20:10.840 --> 00:20:15.080
- Come on, Tracy's right behind us!

00:20:14.240 --> 00:20:16.440
No, she's not!

00:20:15.480 --> 00:20:17.040
- Come on!

00:20:16.080 --> 00:20:18.080
I'll give you a leg up!

00:20:17.400 --> 00:20:19.200
No way!

00:20:18.400 --> 00:20:20.800
It's disgusting!

00:20:20.000 --> 00:20:23.120
I'll give YOU a leg up.

00:20:22.960 --> 00:20:24.880
No, I'll give YOU a leg up.

00:20:24.080 --> 00:20:26.680
Thanks very much!

00:20:25.720 --> 00:20:28.800
Tracy!

00:20:28.000 --> 00:20:31.600
Louise!

00:20:31.000 --> 00:20:34.440
I was only trying to keep my top clean.

00:20:36.360 --> 00:20:37.480
There!

00:20:37.880 --> 00:20:40.560
Now you haven't got anything to worry about!

00:20:39.600 --> 00:20:40.800
Come on!

00:20:44.040 --> 00:20:45.920
Come on!

00:20:44.960 --> 00:20:47.080
Hurry up!

00:20:51.960 --> 00:20:56.080
Stowey House.

00:20:55.320 --> 00:20:57.440
Oh, hello, Elaine.

00:20:56.600 --> 00:21:00.160
Yeah, sorry, I was out earlier.

00:20:59.360 --> 00:21:00.960
Today?

00:21:00.080 --> 00:21:01.480
Well, I guess...

00:21:00.680 --> 00:21:02.440
I am...

00:21:01.520 --> 00:21:03.600
Hang on.

00:21:02.640 --> 00:21:07.960
Lol, Bouncer is NOT a punchbag!

00:21:07.240 --> 00:21:09.840
Sorry about this, Elaine.

00:21:08.880 --> 00:21:12.240
Take those scissors off Dolly!

00:21:11.520 --> 00:21:16.440
Tracy, put that fish back in the fish tank!

00:21:15.480 --> 00:21:18.320
It's crazy around here.

00:21:17.360 --> 00:21:19.440
Can I speak to you later?

00:21:18.480 --> 00:21:20.000
OK.

00:21:20.160 --> 00:21:21.560
Bye.

00:21:20.720 --> 00:21:25.600
Day on my own - it's not too much to ask.

00:21:29.880 --> 00:21:32.400
Not half bad.

00:21:31.680 --> 00:21:34.320
They might just beat us.

00:21:34.400 --> 00:21:38.640
Ohh, hello, Flopsy!

00:21:37.680 --> 00:21:39.520
Aw!

00:21:38.640 --> 00:21:39.800
Eh?!

00:21:39.560 --> 00:21:41.920
The animals!

00:21:41.080 --> 00:21:42.440
Here.

00:21:41.760 --> 00:21:43.000
Warren!

00:21:42.160 --> 00:21:45.600
WARREN!

00:22:01.080 --> 00:22:04.400
What do you think you're doing?

00:22:03.600 --> 00:22:07.600
Shut that gate now!

00:22:06.680 --> 00:22:08.120
Dolly!

00:22:07.160 --> 00:22:08.400
Hah!

00:22:07.440 --> 00:22:11.640
That's the wrong way!

00:22:10.920 --> 00:22:12.640
She doesn't stand a hope now!

00:22:12.920 --> 00:22:17.280
The stock's over half this field!

00:22:16.360 --> 00:22:20.280
Are you just plain stupid?!

00:22:19.880 --> 00:22:24.680
I know what you do, nugget man!

00:22:23.760 --> 00:22:25.000
Eh?

00:22:24.040 --> 00:22:25.560
What do you know?

00:22:24.720 --> 00:22:27.840
City kids don't know the half of it!

00:22:27.000 --> 00:22:31.720
Leave her alone, you big bully!

00:22:30.920 --> 00:22:33.480
I'm not scared of you!

00:22:32.600 --> 00:22:35.120
I did it, all right?!

00:22:34.200 --> 00:22:36.080
I let the animals out!

00:22:35.240 --> 00:22:37.680
What are you gonna do about it?!

00:22:37.960 --> 00:22:40.600
Dad, it's OK.

00:22:39.800 --> 00:22:43.560
Just help me round them up, eh?

00:22:42.680 --> 00:22:45.080
I'm not finished with YOU!

00:22:47.960 --> 00:22:49.960
Thanks.

00:22:49.160 --> 00:22:51.840
You were scary.

00:22:50.880 --> 00:22:52.400
That's OK.

00:23:09.800 --> 00:23:13.960
- Elaine!

00:23:13.040 --> 00:23:17.840
What are you doing here?

00:23:16.960 --> 00:23:21.200
I came to see if I could help.

00:23:20.320 --> 00:23:21.640
- So kind.

00:23:20.680 --> 00:23:21.760
- Don't mention it.

00:23:20.920 --> 00:23:24.960
Professional women have to stick together.

00:23:24.440 --> 00:23:28.880
The thing is, Nathan and Duke have taken the kids out.

00:23:27.960 --> 00:23:30.840
To save me from losing my mind.

00:23:30.680 --> 00:23:36.280
Oh, Jenny, you deserve a medal, you really do.

00:23:35.440 --> 00:23:37.240
Yeah, well...

00:23:36.360 --> 00:23:37.680
I'll see you later.

00:23:36.760 --> 00:23:38.440
OK.

00:23:37.480 --> 00:23:38.680
Bye.

00:23:42.800 --> 00:23:46.080
I just thought!

00:23:45.200 --> 00:23:47.840
Perfect!

00:23:46.880 --> 00:23:53.920
I've got all these case notes to go through and there's no-one here to disturb us!

00:24:00.720 --> 00:24:01.840
Wheeeeeeeeeeeeee!

00:24:01.040 --> 00:24:04.200
Wahooooooo!

00:24:03.360 --> 00:24:04.640
We did it!

00:24:03.680 --> 00:24:06.080
We did it!

00:24:05.120 --> 00:24:06.520
We are the champions!

00:24:05.720 --> 00:24:08.280
We are the champions!

00:24:07.320 --> 00:24:08.800
Oh, yeah!

00:24:08.000 --> 00:24:10.760
Oh, yeah!

00:24:10.440 --> 00:24:12.080
I'm having a re-start.

00:24:11.200 --> 00:24:15.720
I could beat your time with a bucket on my head!

00:24:14.880 --> 00:24:16.120
Justine...wait for me!

00:24:22.640 --> 00:24:28.880
GO!

00:24:31.800 --> 00:24:32.880
Come on, Tracy!

00:24:43.200 --> 00:24:49.280
THEY SHOUT ENCOURAGEMENT SHOUTS OF ENCOURAGEMENT Come on!

00:24:48.320 --> 00:24:49.560
Come on, Tracy!

00:24:51.000 --> 00:24:56.160
Now, I've got a bone to pick with you, little miss.

00:24:56.320 --> 00:24:57.760
Um...

00:24:56.960 --> 00:25:01.640
Hang on, now, be careful!

00:25:00.840 --> 00:25:03.080
See ya!

00:25:08.080 --> 00:25:11.320
CHEERING And we have a winner!

00:25:10.400 --> 00:25:11.760
Yes, yes!

00:25:10.960 --> 00:25:13.120
Ha ha ha ha-ha!

00:25:12.200 --> 00:25:15.160
You've unleashed your potential!

00:25:16.920 --> 00:25:19.000
- OI!

00:25:18.480 --> 00:25:22.360
Sorry, you just need to chill out.

00:25:23.440 --> 00:25:27.960
Thanks for the tour.

00:25:27.040 --> 00:25:28.320
No problem.

00:25:28.200 --> 00:25:30.520
Call me.

00:25:29.800 --> 00:25:31.680
Ooooooooh!

00:25:31.680 --> 00:25:35.720
OK, now, people, let's roll!

00:25:34.880 --> 00:25:40.760
That wild cat, I want a word with her!

00:25:39.920 --> 00:25:48.800
We provide new experiences for people who hardly ever leave the country!

00:25:51.880 --> 00:26:04.400
Bye!

00:27:03.640 --> 00:28:03.720
Subtitles by TFL Ltd BBC Broadcast - 2003 I'm Sam, her best friend.

00:28:02.760 --> 00:28:15.600
I'm her best friend too - Toby.
